  "conclusion": "The current factor-quality pipeline evaluates the user-selected raw five-trading-day adjusted return. The price convention is explicitly adjusted-open to adjusted-open, rather than adjusted-close to adjusted-close. Existing 2020-2025 quality artifacts are comparable only within this frozen convention; a close-based label would be a separate label contract and requires independent re-evaluation."
